  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nBolivia\nBolivia*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nBolivia\nVisa regime\nNationals of Bolivia are required to obtain a visa to enter Montenegro.\nVisas may be obtained from diplomatic and consular posts of Montenegro. If you are unable to reach a diplomatic or consular post of Montenegro, you may apply for a visa at the nearest diplomatic or consular post of the Republic of Serbia.\nContact: the Embassy of the Republic of Serbia in Brasilia, the Federative Republic of BrazilAddress: SES Avenida das Nacoes, Qd. 803, Lote 15, CEP 70409-900 Brasilia D.F., BrazilPhone: +5561 / 3223-72-72+5561 / 212 3223-19-94Fax: +5561 / 3223-84-62Email: embaixadaservia@terra.com.br Website: http://www.brasilia.mfa.gov.rs/\nDiplomatic relations\nThe Plurinational State of Bolivia officially recognized Montenegro on October 18, 2010, when diplomatic relations were established.\nThere is no data on foreign trade.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
